<title>UK: UK's Portillo confident of Germany on Eurofighter.</title>
<headline>UK's Portillo confident of Germany on Eurofighter.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>British Defence Secretary Michael Portillo said on Tuesday he was &quot;pretty confident&quot; about Germany's commitment to the four-nation Eurofighter project.</p>
<p>Portillo was speaking after a meeting last week with his German counterpart Volcker Ruehe.</p>
<p>&quot;I am pretty confident now about the attitude of the German administration, but of course it does have to go through the Bundestag, and you can never take parliamentary votes for granted,&quot; Portillo said at question time in parliament.  </p>
<p>Portillo said Ruehe told him Germany expects to make a decision on participation in the production phase of the Eurofighter programme early next year.</p>
<p>The Eurofighter industrial consortium comprises British Aerospace, Daimler Benz Aerospace, Italy's Alenia and Spain's Casa.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 5424086</p>
